export const QUALITY_GROUNDING =
  "TEMPORAL RELATIONS: A temporal construction establishes timing, not a guaranteed interruption, cancellation or delay. Do not teach that consequence as the construction's invariant meaning. A plan to act is not an action already in progress. Describe the two events as coinciding unless the source explicitly says one stopped the other; never silently paraphrase imminence as an ongoing action. If context suggests a causal relation, clearly qualify it as a contextual possibility.\n\nSCENE CONTEXT: Describe what the text establishes. Prefer a neutral inventory of topics or speech acts. For unlabelled alternating subtitles, say that the passage includes a question, an account and a request; do not say the person giving the account also made the request. Treat such role linking as a factual error, not harmless narrative shorthand. A pronoun may plausibly refer to a preceding name without proving identity: retain the pronoun, or qualify the name as a possibility in EVERY dependent field. Unknown caption content is not evidence of visually blurry text, handwriting or an object on screen. Subtitles alone do not establish pointing, gestures or the appearance/legibility of a physical object. An uncertain transcription is unclear source content, not automatically blurry handwriting or an on-screen gesture. Do not label the speaker surprised, angry or disappointed solely from a question or punctuation. Do not link separate unlabelled turns to the same person or assign narrative motives; keep unspecified roles unspecified.\n\nREPORTED SPEECH: An explicitly third-person attribution does not identify the current listener. A quoted request using first person still belongs to the quoted speaker; do not call it the current listener's request. A quote-only unit describes the quoted content, without importing the narrator's reporting action. Distinguish the current narrator, original speaker/requester, addressee and beneficiary. A preceding name does not identify omitted roles or establish who supplied the report. Keep roles unspecified in translations, meanings, contexts AND points unless explicit source evidence establishes them. Do not treat a quotation/hearsay ending as proof that a mentioned person uttered the exact words. No audio is supplied: explain text-supported readings and general pronunciation rules without claiming the actor's actual delivery.";

